> | 4 | 🏦 | Accounts | Accounts list |
> | 5 | ☰ | More | Counterparties, Flows, Installments, Schedules, Assets, Settings |

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Dashboard Charts** — You said to ask about this when we get there. For the initial build I'll scaffold the dashboard with Chart.js but leave chart types as **placeholder slots** until you specify exactly what stats you want. Is this acceptable, or would you like to specify the dashboard charts now?

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **AI Chat Proxy Route** — The Next.js app will have a route at `app/api/chat/route.ts` that proxies requests to your backend's `/api/chat` endpoint. This avoids CORS issues and keeps your backend URL configurable via env vars. The `useChat()` hook will send to `/api/chat` (the Next.js route), which forwards to your backend. Does this approach work for you?

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Chat Customization Options** — You mentioned users can specify "additional options to customize & personalize response." What kind of options do you have in mind? Examples:
> - Risk tolerance selector (conservative / moderate / aggressive)
> - Context selector (budgeting / investing / debt management)
> - Tone preference (formal / casual)
> - Or should the options panel just be a generic key-value form?
>
> I'll build the chat UI with an expandable options panel, but need to know what fields to include.

