## Proposed Changes

### Phase 0: OpenAPI Sync Bootstrap

Before any application code is written, run `openapi-sync` once against the live backend to generate the complete typed API layer.

1. **Install** `openapi-sync` as a dev dependency: `bun add -D openapi-sync`
2. **Create** `openapi.sync.ts` (see Phase 1 → [openapi.sync.ts](#new-openapitsyncts) below)
3. **Run** `bun run api:sync:once` — this fetches the backend OpenAPI JSON and emits:
   - `lib/generated/wellfinanced/types.ts` — all TypeScript interfaces & enums
   - `lib/generated/wellfinanced/endpoints.ts` — typed URL builders
   - `lib/generated/wellfinanced/hooks.ts` — SWR hooks for every endpoint
   - `lib/generated/wellfinanced/clients.ts` — pre-configured base fetch client
4. **Commit** the generated files so the rest of the team can start immediately without running the sync
5. **Add** `.gitignore` rule to **not** ignore `lib/generated/` (generated files are intentionally committed)

> [!NOTE]
> The `refetchInterval: 30_000` setting in `openapi.sync.ts` means the watcher auto-regenerates when the backend schema changes during development. No manual re-runs needed.

