#### [NEW] [openapi.sync.ts](file:///d:/Downloads/selected-project/openapi.sync.ts)

`openapi-sync` configuration file — the single source of truth for all API codegen:

```ts
import type { IConfig } from 'openapi-sync/types';

const config: IConfig = {
  // In dev, poll every 30 s so types stay fresh as the backend evolves.
  // Set to 0 in CI / production to disable auto-fetch.
  refetchInterval: process.env.NODE_ENV === 'development' ? 30_000 : 0,

  // Output directory — committed to git (reviewed like any other generated code)
  folder: './lib/generated',

  api: {
    wellfinanced:
      'https://kamarshalaby0--wellfinanced-fastapi-app.modal.run/api/v1/openapi.json',
  },

  // SWR hooks — aligned with the existing useApi.ts data-fetching pattern
  clientGeneration: {
    type: 'swr',
    baseURL: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL ??
      'https://kamarshalaby0--wellfinanced-fastapi-app.modal.run',
  },

  // Split generated files by OpenAPI tag → one sub-folder per resource
  folderSplit: { byTags: true },

  // Prefix every interface with `I` for instant visual distinction
  types: { name: { prefix: 'I', useOperationId: true } },

  // Exclude internal / docs routes from the generated client
  endpoints: {
    exclude: { tags: ['docs', 'redoc', 'openapi'] },
  },
};

export default config;
```

**What gets generated** (inside `lib/generated/wellfinanced/`):

| File | Contents |
|---|---|
| `types.ts` | All TypeScript interfaces — `IAccount`, `IInflow`, `IOutflow`, enums, DTOs, pagination wrappers |
| `endpoints.ts` | Typed URL builders: `getAccounts()`, `getAccountById(id)`, … |
| `hooks.ts` | SWR hooks: `useGetAccounts()`, `useGetAccountById(id)`, `useCreateAccount()`, … |
| `clients.ts` | Base fetch client pre-configured with `baseURL` and response-envelope unwrapping |

**NPM scripts** added to `package.json`:

```json
"scripts": {
  "api:sync": "openapi-sync",
  "api:sync:once": "openapi-sync --no-watch"
}
```

Run `bun run api:sync:once` once during Phase 0 to bootstrap the generated files, then the watcher keeps them current during development.

